<task id="031" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Generic typed-intake framework (typed form → submit → status)</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:022,030</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New framework surface spanning client (React/Fluent v9) + BFF (new endpoint group); base others (032/033/035) build on; tags include bff-api + frontend — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural: defines the reusable intake framework contract (config-driven request types, form → submit → status pipeline, BFF endpoint-group shape) that must not foreclose future types; high blast radius across P3.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Framework base that 032 (NDA), 033 (P&amp;P), and 035 (my-requests) all extend/consume; must land and stabilize before those; touches the shared external-access BFF surface (conflict-check with teams-app-r1).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>022,030</deps>
    <tags>frontend, bff-api, api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Build the reusable Legal Front Door typed-intake framework: a config-driven client flow (pick request type → typed form → review → submit → status/confirmation) built ONLY on @spaarke/ui-components WizardModal (multi-step types) / FormModal (single-step types), plus a per-module BFF endpoint group (MapFrontDoorEndpoints) that persists a sprk_servicerequest and returns its status. Adding a new request type must be config/schema + a form, not a new app (FR-14).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Fluent v9 + React 18 on the shared component library; ASP.NET Minimal API endpoint groups with ADR-008 route-group filters and ADR-019 ProblemDetails.</role>
  <goal>A generic intake framework exists: (1) client — a typed-intake driver that renders a request type's schema through WizardModal/FormModal, submits it, and shows status, wired into the external-spa module-host shell; (2) BFF — a MapFrontDoorEndpoints group under the external-access surface that creates a sprk_servicerequest (requester/type/status from 030) and exposes submit + get-status. NDA (032) and P&amp;P (033) plug in as config + a form with no framework change.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-14: A reusable intake module framework the request types plug into (typed form → submit → status); adding a new request type is config/schema + a form, not a new app. UX brief §3 "Legal Front Door — typed intake": WizardModal multi-step (pick type → typed form → review → submit → confirmation); single-step types use FormModal; prototype seed multi-step-dialog-variant-template.tsx. §11 shared-library mandate: no hand-rolled dialogs. FR-13 (030) supplies the sprk_servicerequest intake fields this framework writes. FR-22/teams-app-r1: per-module endpoint groups over CallerPrincipalResolver — this framework's endpoints are the Front Door module group; the requester==caller Tier-2 predicate and app-only upload are added in 034 (this task establishes the group + submit/status; 034 hardens authz + upload).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md (§3 typed intake row + §4 nine required states)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts:273 (SprkModal presets export: WizardModal, FormModal, ConfirmModal, PreviewModal)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/registry/WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts (lazy-factory registry pattern to adopt for request-type registration)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/App.tsx, src/client/external-spa/src/pages/WorkspaceHomePage.tsx (module-host shell to mount the intake flow into)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs (/api/v1/external group :56 — reference for MapFrontDoorEndpoints shape)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs:29 (group-level ADR-008 filter to reuse)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (plane-agnostic caller; CallerPrincipal :66)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (binding BFF governance — Placement Justification + publish size)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>022 (accessible-record-set / entitlement wiring) and 030 (sprk_servicerequest intake fields) must be complete. 032/033 depend on this; 034 hardens the Tier-2 predicate + upload on this group; 035 renders the list.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">ALL intake dialogs MUST be built from @spaarke/ui-components SprkModal presets — WizardModal for multi-step request types, FormModal for single-step. Do NOT hand-roll a Dialog or fork LegalWorkspaceApp (§11 + ADR-050). The typed-form rendering must be config-driven so a request type = a schema + a form.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The Front Door BFF endpoints MUST be a single route-group (MapFrontDoorEndpoints) with a group-level authorization filter (reuse CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter) — no per-endpoint ad-hoc middleware, no global middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">All BFF error responses MUST use ProblemDetails; no bare status codes or custom error envelopes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Introduce an interface only where ≥2 real implementations exist; register concretes otherwise. The request-type registry may be an interface/config seam (multiple request types), but do not add speculative single-impl abstractions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF addition: state the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); run dotnet publish -c Release and report compressed size + delta vs baseline 46.90 MB incl PDBs (ceiling ≤60 MB); run /conflict-check before the BFF PR (teams-app-r1 shares Api/ExternalAccess/** + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only (makeStyles/tokens); zero hardcoded hex/shadow; verified in light, dark, and Teams theme; the flow must render in a narrow Teams personal-tab width.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
