    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Lazy registry" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/registry/WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts">Adopt the lazy-factory registry pattern for registering request types { id, title, formSchema/lazyForm }.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Endpoint group" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs">Mirror the /api/v1/external group :56 to author MapFrontDoorEndpoints with a group-level filter.</pattern>
      <pattern name="SprkModal presets" location="docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md">WizardModal for multi-step, FormModal for single-step; Cancel always left; scaled Fluent theme.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec.md FR-14/FR-22, ux-brief.md §3/§4, ADR-008/019/050, MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md, and bff-extensions.md. Run /conflict-check for the external-access BFF surface.</step>
    <step order="2">Client: define a request-type registry ({ id, title, mode: 'wizard'|'form', form/schema, lazyLoader }) adopting the WorkspaceWidgetRegistry lazy pattern. Register a placeholder type to prove the seam (NDA/P&amp;P land in 032/033).</step>
    <step order="3">Client: build the typed-intake driver that, given a request-type id, renders its form through WizardModal (multi-step: pick type → typed form → review → submit → confirmation) or FormModal (single-step), submits to the BFF, and shows submit result/status. No hand-rolled Dialog.</step>
    <step order="4">Client: mount the intake entry point in the external-spa module-host shell (WorkspaceHomePage/App). Implement the nine required states (loading, empty, error, unentitled/denied, dark, Teams theme, keyboard-only, narrow width) per ux-brief §4.</step>
    <step order="5">BFF: author MapFrontDoorEndpoints as a route-group under the external-access surface with a group-level CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. Endpoints: POST submit (create sprk_servicerequest with requester/type/status from 030) and GET status/by-id. Register services as concretes (ADR-010). ProblemDetails for errors.</step>
    <step order="6">BFF: resolve the caller via CallerPrincipalResolver and set requester (lazy Contact attribution is fully implemented in 034 — here, wire the resolver + persist the request; leave the requester==caller enforcement + app-only upload as the 034 hardening seam, clearly marked).</step>
    <step order="7">Tests: add KEEP-path integration tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ for submit + get-status (real endpoint-group wiring). NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests (ADR-038). Add client component tests for the driver rendering a type through WizardModal/FormModal.</step>
    <step order="8">Build: npm run build:prod for the client; dotnet publish -c Release for BFF — report compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline. State the Placement Justification in the task notes / PR body.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/** — request-type registry + typed-intake driver (WizardModal/FormModal) mounted in the shell</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** — MapFrontDoorEndpoints group (submit + get-status) with group-level filter</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/** — KEEP-path integration tests for submit + status; client component tests for the driver</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a registered request type, when a user opens intake, then the typed form renders inside a WizardModal (multi-step) or FormModal (single-step) from @spaarke/ui-components — no hand-rolled Dialog in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a completed typed form, when the user submits, then POST to MapFrontDoorEndpoints creates a sprk_servicerequest with requester + type + status and returns a status the client renders as a confirmation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a new (hypothetical) request type, when it is added, then it requires only a registry entry + a form/schema — no change to the framework driver or the endpoint group (FR-14 closed set: config/schema + a form, not a new app).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an unauthenticated/denied caller, when hitting the Front Door endpoints, then the group-level filter returns a ProblemDetails 401/403 — no request is created (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the BFF build, when dotnet publish -c Release runs, then compressed size is reported with delta vs 46.90 MB and is ≤60 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the intake flow, when rendered in light, dark, and Teams theme at narrow width, then semantic tokens adapt with zero hardcoded hex and no console errors.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
    <existing>No existing intake framework — grep of src/client/external-spa and src/client/shared finds a widget/tab registry (WorkspaceWidgetRegistry) and modal presets, but no "pick type → typed form → submit → status" driver and no Front Door BFF endpoint group. sprk_servicerequest is a stub extended by 030.</existing>
    <extension>No — the driver + endpoint group are net-new, but they are COMPOSED from existing surface (WizardModal/FormModal, the WorkspaceWidgetRegistry pattern, CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter, the /api/v1/external group shape). We reuse patterns and primitives, not fork them.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the framework, each request type (NDA, P&amp;P, future) would be a hand-copied SPA + a bespoke endpoint — the exact drift the §11 gate forbids; adding a request type would be a new app instead of config + a form (FR-14 fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Renders typed intake">
      <steps><step>Open the intake entry point in the external-spa shell</step><step>Pick the registered request type; step through WizardModal (or FormModal for single-step)</step><step>Submit</step></steps>
      <expected>Form renders inside the SprkModal preset; submit returns a confirmation/status; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode via ThemeToggle</step><step>Load inside a Teams-theme host (light/dark/high-contrast)</step><step>Verify semantic tokens adapt</step></steps>
      <expected>Zero hardcoded hex; tokens adapt across light/dark/Teams; readable at narrow Teams personal-tab width</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Unentitled/denied state">
      <steps><step>Simulate a caller without Front Door entitlement</step><step>Attempt to open intake / submit</step></steps>
      <expected>Denied state shown client-side; server returns ProblemDetails 401/403; no sprk_servicerequest created</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Spec FR-14 + FR-22. UX brief §3 (typed intake) + §4 (nine states). This task establishes the framework + endpoint group + submit/status; 034 adds the requester==caller Tier-2 predicate + app-only SPE upload; 035 renders my-requests. Prototype seed: multi-step-dialog-variant-template.tsx. §10 BFF: Placement Justification + publish size + conflict-check are mandatory. Use build:prod (NOT build) for the client per CLAUDE.md §12 / AP-1.</notes>
